  "zh": "# OpenAI 发布 GPT-6 引发 AGI 时代讨论，多款大模型同日宕机\n\n## AI 与科技\n- **GPT-6 Astra 发布**：OpenAI 宣称进入 AGI 时代，实测能处理复杂多步推理任务，引发「真 AGI 假炒作」激辩。\n- **多款 AI 大模型集体宕机**：OpenAI、Claude、Grok 同时间段服务中断，用户遭遇史上最大范围 AI 停摆。\n- **通义千问 3.8 27B 登陆 Cerebras**：每秒 1500 token 推理速度刷新纪录，国产开源模型性能逼近头部闭源模型。\n\n## 行业动向\n- **大众汽车计划再裁 5 万人**：德国车企转型电动化阵痛持续，全球汽车就业市场承压。\n- **长鑫存储 DRAM 份额升至 10%**：国产内存芯片加速替代韩美厂商，存储自主化迈出关键一步。\n- **特斯拉 Cybercab 无人出租车上市**：自动驾驶商业化落地进程受到市场密切关注。\n\n## 国际与社会\n- **多国从美国运回黄金储备**：波兰、德国等国持续 repatriate 黄金，美元信用体系面临长期挑战。\n- **亚运会中国体育代表团成立**：亚洲最大综合性运动会即将开幕，中国队备战进入冲刺阶段。\n\n## 开发者圈\n- **Audacity 4.0 正式发布**：开源音频编辑器迎重大更新，跨平台插件生态进一步增强。",
  "en": "# OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra Sparks AGI Debate as Multiple AI Models Crash Simultaneously\n\n## AI & Tech\n- **GPT-6 Astra Released**: OpenAI declares the arrival of the AGI era, with the model acing complex multi-step reasoning tasks—prompting fierce debate over hype vs. substance.\n- **OpenAI, Claude, and Grok All Went Down**: Simultaneous outages hit the three major AI providers in what users are calling the biggest AI blackout ever.\n- **Qwen 3.8 27B Hits Cerebras**: The open-weight Chinese model now runs at 1,500 tokens/s, rivaling closed-source giants on speed.\n\n## Industry & Markets\n- **Volkswagen Plans 50,000 More Layoffs**: The German automaker's EV transition continues to bleed jobs globally.\n- **Longxin DRAM Market Share Hits 10%**: China's homegrown memory chip maker gains ground on Samsung and SK Hynix.\n- **Tesla Cybercab Robotaxi Launches**: Autonomous vehicle commercial deployment enters a critical market test phase.\n\n## Global Affairs\n- **Nations Repatriating Gold From the US**: Poland, Germany and others quietly moving reserves home, signaling eroding trust in dollar-denominated assets.\n- **Asian Games Chinese Delegation Formed**: The continent's biggest multi-sport event is weeks away, with China's team locked in final preparations.\n\n## Developer World\n- **Audacity 4.0 Ships**: The open-source audio editor gets its biggest overhaul, with improved cross-platform plugin support."
